Trust Calculation Formula
Aggregate Trust = (user_trust × 0.4) + (device_trust × 0.4) + ((1 - app_risk) × 0.2)

Weights: User (40%) • Device (40%) • Application (20%)

Key Policy Insights
Absolute Rules:

Blacklisted users are always denied (highest priority)

Admin status provides privilege but still requires minimum trust

Trust Thresholds:

Full Access: ≥ 0.75 (admins only)

Limited Access: ≥ 0.45 (all users)

No Access: < 0.45 (all users)

Impact Factors:

High-risk applications significantly reduce aggregate trust

Device trust is equally weighted as user trust

Low user trust cannot be fully compensated by other factors

Decision Logic Flow:

text
1. Is user blacklisted? → Deny
2. Calculate aggregate trust
3. Is user admin AND trust ≥ 0.75? → Full access
4. Is trust ≥ 0.45? → Limited access
5. Default → No access
